LICENSE

The C11 editor uses GPLv3, as recorded in ROADMAP.md, with the full text in
LICENSE. libtam (https://github.com/greenermoose/libtam) also uses GPLv3.
micro's MIT permission notice is kept in LICENSE-MIT and covers the
runtime data and the other parts that come from micro; LICENSE-THIRD-PARTY
carries the notices for the third-party libraries micro uses.


UPSTREAM

micro's own documentation -- every option, command, keybinding and plugin --
is at https://micro-editor.github.io and in micro-editor/micro
(https://github.com/micro-editor/micro). ideas/sources lists a full
clone of micro under ~/Code/micro, which tools/pull-references keeps up
to date; runtime/help/ here answers most questions too.

The parts of micro's Go source worth reading before porting a feature:

  Buffer, cursors, undo, save, search:
    internal/buffer/ -- buffer.go, cursor.go, eventhandler.go, save.go,
    search.go
  Commands, keybindings, panes, tabs:
    internal/action/ -- actions.go, bindings.go, command.go, pane.go
  Settings, colorschemes, runtime files:
    internal/config/ -- settings.go, colorscheme.go, rtfiles.go
  Drawing, statusline, soft wrap:
    internal/display/
  Highlighting state machine:
    pkg/highlight/ -- highlighter.go, parser.go
  Lua plugin API (deferred):
    internal/lua/
  Syntax definitions and colours:
    runtime/syntax/, runtime/colorschemes/

Bug reports and fixes come from micro's issue tracker
(https://github.com/micro-editor/micro/issues). git log in the micro clone
records what was fixed and why.
